// FAQ data
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Will a kill switch disconnect me from video calls?',
    answer: '<p>Only if your VPN connection drops. A properly functioning kill switch sits dormant while your VPN works normally. You won\'t notice it\'s there.</p><p>If your VPN does disconnect (server issue, network problem, etc.), yes—the kill switch will cut your video call to prevent data exposure. But consider: would you rather have your call interrupted or have your real IP and potentially sensitive data exposed?</p><p>Modern premium VPNs have stable connections. VPN drops are rare—maybe a few times per year. The protection is worth the small risk of occasional interruption.</p>'
