    answer: '<p><strong>Yes, keep it enabled.</strong> There\'s no downside when your VPN is working properly. The kill switch only activates when something goes wrong—which is exactly when you need protection most.</p><p>Some users disable kill switch when they need guaranteed connectivity (live streaming, important presentations). But for normal remote work, leave it on. A brief disconnection is better than exposed data.</p>'
