    answer: '<p>Yes, but implementation varies:</p><ul><li><strong>Android:</strong> Supports app-level and system-level kill switches. Android also has native "Block connections without VPN" in settings—use both.</li><li><strong>iOS:</strong> More limited due to Apple restrictions. Most iOS VPN apps use "On Demand" rules to auto-reconnect, but true kill switch functionality is constrained. iOS VPNs reconnect quickly rather than blocking all traffic.</li></ul><p>Android offers better kill switch protection; iOS users should ensure auto-reconnect is enabled.</p>'
